{
  "dom_id": "step-q161463",
  "name": "Question 1",
  "problem": "For a surface $S$ given by $z=g(x,y)$ for $(x,y)\\in D,$ the flux of the vector field $F(x,y,z)=⟨P,\\,Q,\\,R⟩$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{D}(-P\\frac{∂g}{\\bbox[3pt,border:1pt solid black]{\\phantom{A}}}-Q\\frac{∂g}{\\bbox[3pt,border:1pt solid black]{\\phantom{A}}}+R)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nFrom left to right, what are the missing parts of the formula?",
